  <front>
    <title abbrev="checksum window">A checksum over a window</title>
    <seriesInfo name="Internet-Draft" value="draft-checksum-window-00"/>
    <author initials="V." surname="Fixture" fullname="Vector Fixture">
      <organization>vector</organization>
      <address>
      </address>
    </author>
    <date year="2026" month="November" day="19"/>
    <abstract>
      <?line 13?>

<t>A fixture, not a specification: CRC-32 and Adler-32 over a window of a
buffer, as nish's std checksum takes them, from spec to a run of that
module. Each function takes its bytes as
(buf, off, len), which the interface declares as one bytes parameter.</t>
    </abstract>
  </front>
  <middle>
    <?line 20?>

<section anchor="introduction">
      <name>Introduction</name>
      <t>The key words "<bcp14>MUST</bcp14>", "<bcp14>MUST NOT</bcp14>", "<bcp14>REQUIRED</bcp14>", "<bcp14>SHALL</bcp14>", "<bcp14>SHALL
NOT</bcp14>", "<bcp14>SHOULD</bcp14>", "<bcp14>SHOULD NOT</bcp14>", "<bcp14>RECOMMENDED</bcp14>", "<bcp14>NOT RECOMMENDED</bcp14>",
"<bcp14>MAY</bcp14>", and "<bcp14>OPTIONAL</bcp14>" in this document are to be interpreted as
described in BCP 14 <xref target="RFC2119"/> <xref target="RFC8174"/> when, and only when, they
appear in all capitals, as shown here.</t>
      <?line -18?>

<t>The module is nish's own nish/compress/checksum, checked and run with
<tt>--nish-root</tt>. Its tests in tests/spec/emit run the same emitted test
against copies of it with one window read wrong, which the contract
refuses: the test passes every window at a nonzero offset, between guard
bytes.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="interface">
      <name>Interface</name>
      <sourcecode type="ts-interface"><![CDATA[
// module: nish/compress/checksum
export const crc32 = (buf: u8[] /* window */): u32
export const adler32 = (buf: u8[] /* window */): u32
export const adler32Update = (adler: u32, buf: u8[] /* window */): u32
]]></sourcecode>
    </section>
    <section anchor="crc32">
      <name>CRC-32</name>
      <t anchor="R-CRC32">crc32 <bcp14>MUST</bcp14> return the CRC-32 of the window's bytes, the reflected CRC with
polynomial 0xEDB88320 that zlib computes, and only of those bytes.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="adler32">
      <name>Adler-32</name>
      <t anchor="R-ADLER32">adler32 <bcp14>MUST</bcp14> return the Adler-32 of the window's bytes, as zlib computes it,
and only of those bytes.</t>
      <t anchor="R-ADLER32-UPDATE">adler32Update <bcp14>MUST</bcp14> return the Adler-32 of the bytes an earlier checksum
covered followed by the window's bytes.</t>
      <sourcecode type="ts-property"><![CDATA[
// P-ADLER32-SPLIT covers R-ADLER32, R-ADLER32-UPDATE — a checksum continued over a second window is the checksum of both
forall (a: u8[] /* 0..32 */, b: u8[] /* 0..32 */) => adler32Update(adler32(a), b) === adler32(a.concat(b))
]]></sourcecode>
    </section>
    <section anchor="check-values">
      <name>Check values</name>
      <t>These values are what zlib's crc32 and adler32 print in Python 3, as
<tt>python3 -c 'import zlib; print(zlib.crc32(b"123456789"))'</tt> does.</t>
      <t>The CRC-32 of "123456789" is Check = 3421780262, and of "" it is Zero = 0.</t>
      <t>The Adler-32 of "Wikipedia" is Adler = 300286872, and of "" it is Initial = 1.</t>
      <t>The Adler-32 of "abc" continued from Start = 300286872 is Continued = 519570622.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="security-considerations">
      <name>Security Considerations</name>
      <t>Neither checksum resists a deliberate change: both detect accidental errors
only.</t>
    </section>
